  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Fifth changes hands",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "ｶﾎｳｼｭｳｾｲ reached fifth at 72.50 after a recorded transition from tenth at 70.28. The move lifts it above _hans and Majkel1337, now sixth and seventh, both at 71.81. It is the clearest reshuffle among the leading contenders this morning.\n\nTufa Labs still leads at 88.06, with Yi-Chia Chen second at 84.72. Third-place rabbithole advances from 80.56 to 80.83 in the recorded overnight event, while nvbanana stays fourth at 79.17. The event establishes that improvement; the missing midnight comparison for rabbithole remains unknown."
    },
    {
      "heading": "One place from gold",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-19-2158-arc-2-gold-cutoff-rises-okiek-outside"
      ],
      "text": "matu997 closes 17th at 64.31 after the recorded jump from 54.58 and 23rd. The provisional gold line remains 64.72, leaving a gap of 0.41 points. okiek, the subject of the earlier wire report, is now 18th at 63.47.\n\nThe wire described a rise in the gold cutoff over its longer window. The Early edition’s midnight and closing snapshots both put it at 64.72: the new development is matu997’s approach, not another rise in that boundary. Public medal places can still change."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Cole confirms the ARC Mutants move",
      "sourceIds": [
        "person-jack-cole-identity-0",
        "social-2112303089198022857",
        "fact-17023174-0",
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Jack Cole has publicly confirmed joining Mark Barney’s ARC-AGI-2 team, saying he is excited and that they will work hard through the final two weeks because the competition is strong. The closing ARC Mutants roster lists jcole75, markbarney, scizical and sonphamorg. The team remains 56th at 39.31, unchanged against the midnight comparison.\n\nThis is ARC2 team 17023174. It is separate from ARC3 Team Turducken; Cole’s announcement supplies no ARC3 membership change and no evidence that a new score has already followed."
    }
